# Step 28, the loop's hook seam: `cineris_agent::Hooks` at `prompt.submit`
# and `tool.before` (docs/steps/28/answered.md, "6. Hooks in the loop").
# Each rule broken one at a time, with the tests that must fail. Breaks
# whose only symptom is a wait that never ends are caught when the test's
# time runs out.

[break] a-tool-point-lists-hooks-nobody-wants
rule: With no hook whose filter matches a call, the point is passed on the cheap check: no hook is even listed.
file: crates/cineris-agent/src/round.rs
in: Planning::hooked
find: narrowable && set.hooks.wants(HookEvent::ToolBefore, Some(target))
replace: narrowable
caught-by:
    cineris-agent::it hooks::with_no_hook_that_matches_every_point_is_passed_and_nothing_changes

[break] a-prompt-point-lists-hooks-nobody-wants
rule: With no `prompt.submit` hook, a prompt and a steering message pass at once: no hook is even listed.
file: crates/cineris-agent/src/turn.rs
in: Session::wants_prompts
find: .is_some_and(|set| set.hooks.wants(HookEvent::PromptSubmit, None))
replace: .is_some()
caught-by:
    cineris-agent::it hooks::with_no_hook_that_matches_every_point_is_passed_and_nothing_changes

